From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:10:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: preserve DSA tag for PPPoE

PPPoE discovery over a tag_8021q DSA user port works before the PPP
channel is connected.  The channel notifier then creates a VLAN uplink
for the DSA standalone VID with keep_tag disabled.  Its ingress
translation deletes the service tag from all subsequent packets in that
VID, including PPPoE session traffic punted to the CPU.  The DSA receive
path can no longer recover the source port, so LCP packets are dropped
and negotiation times out.

Record when the PPPoE path's VLAN is a tag_8021q DSA service tag and
retain it when creating the session uplink.  Ordinary VLAN PPPoE still
terminates its customer tag, while QCA4B DSA paths continue to carry
port identity outside the VLAN header.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
@@ -694,6 +694,7 @@ struct ppe_ft_pppoe_topo {
 	int vlan_mtu;
 	int port;
 	int vid;
+	bool keep_tag;
 };
 
 static int ppe_ft_vlan_get(struct ppe_flowtable *ft, int port, u16 vid,
@@ -762,8 +763,10 @@ static int ppe_ft_pppoe_path(struct net_
 				ret = dsa_mode;
 				goto out_unlock;
 			}
-			if (dsa_mode == PPE_FT_DSA_TAG_8021Q)
+			if (dsa_mode == PPE_FT_DSA_TAG_8021Q) {
 				topo->vid = vid;
+				topo->keep_tag = true;
+			}
 			topo->vlan_mtu = path->dev->mtu;
 			ether_addr_copy(topo->local, path->dev->dev_addr);
 			break;
@@ -893,7 +896,7 @@ static int ppe_ft_pppoe_connect(struct p
 	mutex_lock(&ft->lock);
 	if (topo.vid >= 0) {
 		vlan = ppe_ft_vlan_get(ft, topo.port, topo.vid, topo.vlan_mtu,
-				       false);
+				       topo.keep_tag);
 		if (vlan < 0) {
 			ret = vlan;
 			goto out_unlock;
